; tests/str-byte-at-band.fk — sibling-witness band for the Form-native raw-byte accessor.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/str-byte-at.fk
;
; Proves str-byte-at (and the big-endian decoders that compose on it) read the same raw bytes on every
; kernel. The four ASCII claims came first; the header used to explain the choice as "ASCII literals so
; each byte is its codepoint and the verdict is deterministic across the four walkers".
;
; THAT SENTENCE IS WHY THIS HID. The cell exists for binary framing — pg-wire, gguf, base64, hex — and
; binary framing lives above 127. Restricting the band to ASCII made the verdict deterministic by
; confining it to the one input range where the old implementation could not fail. It read 15 on every
; arm for as long as it has existed, while (str-byte-at "λ" 0) was 206 on fkwu and -1 on go, rust and ts.
; The non-ASCII claims below are the coverage that would have caught it, added 2026-07-26 with the repair.
;   1    str-byte-at "ABCD" 0 == 65 (A)
;   2    str-byte-at "ABCD" 3 == 68 (D)
;   4    str-be16 "AB"   == 16706         (65*256 + 66)
;   8    str-be32 "ABCD" == 1094861636    (65*2^24 + 66*2^16 + 67*2^8 + 68)
;   16   two-byte glyph, first byte:  str-byte-at "λ" 0 == 206   (0xCE)
;   32   two-byte glyph, second byte: str-byte-at "λ" 1 == 187   (0xBB)
;   64   str-be16 over that glyph == 52923                       (206*256 + 187)
;   128  three-byte glyph: str-byte-at "€" 2 == 172              (0xE2 0x82 0xAC)
;   256  str_len counts BYTES, not characters: str_len "λ€" == 5
; Verdict 511 when every claim lands.
(do
    (let c0 (if (eq (str-byte-at "ABCD" 0) 65) 1 0))
    (let c1 (if (eq (str-byte-at "ABCD" 3) 68) 2 0))
    (let c2 (if (eq (str-be16 "AB" 0) 16706) 4 0))
    (let c3 (if (eq (str-be32 "ABCD" 0) 1094861636) 8 0))
    (let c4 (if (eq (str-byte-at "λ" 0) 206) 16 0))
    (let c5 (if (eq (str-byte-at "λ" 1) 187) 32 0))
    (let c6 (if (eq (str-be16 "λ" 0) 52923) 64 0))
    (let c7 (if (eq (str-byte-at "€" 2) 172) 128 0))
    (let c8 (if (eq (str_len "λ€") 5) 256 0))
    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 (add c3 (add c4 (add c5 (add c6 (add c7 c8)))))))))
